---
import AtlasRelationship from "../../components/AtlasRelationship.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getAtlas } from "../../lib/atlas-data";
const atlas = getAtlas();
---
<BaseLayout title="Relationship and source register — LLM Lineage" description="Complete source-located evidence for every recorded relationship in the selected language-model research corpus." eyebrow="Atlas evidence">
  <header class="shell atlas-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Shared evidence · two learning paths</p>
    <h1>Read what a connection actually establishes.</h1>
    <p>Every recorded relationship keeps its independent fields, bound claims, source locators and interpretation limits. The source register below serves both catalogues.</p>
    <nav class="atlas-section-nav" aria-label="Evidence navigation"><a href="/atlas/beginner/">Beginner catalogue</a><a href="/atlas/expert/">Expert catalogue</a><a href="/atlas/lenses/">Compare evidence lenses</a><a href="#relationships">Relationships</a><a href="#sources">Source register</a></nav>
  </header>
  <section class="shell atlas-relationships" id="relationships" aria-labelledby="relations-heading">
    <div class="atlas-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Scoped evidence, not a universal chain</p><h2 id="relations-heading">{atlas.counts.relationships} recorded relationships.</h2><p>The three fields are independent. Connection type names the relationship; evidential basis describes its support; causal permission limits its wording. No transitive influence is inferred.</p></div>
    <dl class="atlas-evidence-key">
      <div><dt><span class="atlas-line atlas-line--documented-influence" aria-hidden="true"></span>Documented influence · {atlas.counts.evidenceClass["documented-influence"]}</dt><dd>Solid rule: target-documented evidence. This class can still prohibit causal wording.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><span class="atlas-line atlas-line--inherited-mechanism" aria-hidden="true"></span>Inherited mechanism · {atlas.counts.evidenceClass["inherited-mechanism"]}</dt><dd>Dotted rule: a scoped shared mechanism, without automatically establishing a direct influence path.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><span class="atlas-line atlas-line--editorial-synthesis" aria-hidden="true"></span>Editorial synthesis · {atlas.counts.evidenceClass["editorial-synthesis"]}</dt><dd>Dashed rule: a reviewed editorial bridge or comparison. Read its causal restriction.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="atlas-boundary">{atlas.counts.causalLanguage["qualified"]} records permit qualified wording; {atlas.counts.causalLanguage["prohibited"]} prohibit causal language. Line patterns encode evidence class, not confidence or importance. Stored from/to endpoints show record orientation. No causal arrows are drawn in this text index.</p>
    {atlas.relationships.map((relation) => <AtlasRelationship relation={relation} />)}
  </section>
  <section class="shell atlas-sources" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-heading">
    <div class="atlas-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">First-party and curated contextual evidence</p><h2 id="sources-heading">Source register · {atlas.sources.length} records</h2><p>Each locator above names a source here. Access notes distinguish complete texts, metadata, restrictions, versions and third-party reading copies. A verification date describes a targeted check, not field completeness.</p></div>
    {atlas.sources.map((source) => <article class="atlas-source" id={`source-${source.id}`}><details class="atlas-disclosure"><summary>{source.title}<small>{source.id}</small></summary><div class="atlas-detail-body"><a href={source.url} rel="noreferrer">Open source: {source.title}</a><p class="atlas-small atlas-source-url">{source.url}</p><p class="atlas-small">{source.sourceClass} · {source.authority} · accessed {source.accessDate}</p><p>{source.accessNote}</p><p class="atlas-small">Version scope: {source.versionIds.length > 0 ? source.versionIds.join(", ") : "Work-level or contextual evidence; no version binding"}</p><p class="atlas-small">Related works: {source.relatedWorkIds.map((id) => <a class="atlas-inline-source" href={`/atlas/expert/#work-${id}`}>{id}</a>)}</p><a href="/atlas/expert/#catalogue">Return to catalogue navigation ↑</a></div></details></article>)}
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
